  40:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                                      CHANGE PRIORITY OF A TASK
  41:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
  42:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Description: This function allows you to change the priority of a task dynamically.  Note that th
  43:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              priority MUST be available.
  44:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
  45:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Arguments  : oldp     is the old priority
  46:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
  47:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              newp     is the new priority
  48:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
  49:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Returns    : OS_ERR_NONE            is the call was successful
  50:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              OS_ERR_PRIO_INVALID    if the priority you specify is higher that the maximum allowe
  51:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                                     (i.e. >= OS_LOWEST_PRIO)
  52:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              OS_ERR_PRIO_EXIST      if the new priority already exist.
  53:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              OS_ERR_PRIO            there is no task with the specified OLD priority (i.e. the OL
  54:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                                     not exist.
  55:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              OS_ERR_TASK_NOT_EXIST  if the task is assigned to a Mutex PIP.
  56:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  57:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** */
