1118:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** /*
1119:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
1120:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                              GET THE CURRENT VALUE OF A TASK REGISTER
1121:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1122:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Description: This function is called to obtain the current value of a task register.  Task regist
1123:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              are application specific and can be used to store task specific values such as 'erro
1124:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              numbers' (i.e. errno), statistics, etc.  Each task register can hold a 32-bit value.
1125:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1126:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Arguments  : prio      is the priority of the task you want to get the task register from.  If yo
1127:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                        specify OS_PRIO_SELF then the task register of the current task will be ob
1128:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1129:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              id        is the 'id' of the desired task register.  Note that the 'id' must be less
1130:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                        than OS_TASK_REG_TBL_SIZE
1131:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1132:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              perr      is a pointer to a variable that will hold an error code related to this ca
1133:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1134:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                        OS_ERR_NONE            if the call was successful
1135:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                        OS_ERR_PRIO_INVALID    if you specified an invalid priority
1136:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                        OS_ERR_ID_INVALID      if the 'id' is not between 0 and OS_TASK_REG_TBL_SI
1137:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
