1342:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                                          CLEAR TASK STACK
1343:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1344:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Description: This function is used to clear the stack of a task (i.e. write all zeros)
1345:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1346:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Arguments  : pbos     is a pointer to the task's bottom of stack.  If the configuration constant
1347:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       OS_STK_GROWTH is set to 1, the stack is assumed to grow downward (i.e. from
1348:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       memory to low memory).  'pbos' will thus point to the lowest (valid) memory
1349:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       location of the stack.  If OS_STK_GROWTH is set to 0, 'pbos' will point to 
1350:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       highest memory location of the stack and the stack will grow with increasin
1351:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       memory locations.  'pbos' MUST point to a valid 'free' data item.
1352:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1353:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              size     is the number of 'stack elements' to clear.
1354:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1355:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *              opt      contains additional information (or options) about the behavior of the task
1356:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       LOWER 8-bits are reserved by uC/OS-II while the upper 8 bits can be applica
1357:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *                       specific.  See OS_TASK_OPT_??? in uCOS-II.H.
1358:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** *
1359:./ucos/Core/os_task.c **** * Returns    : none
